OL,3,GNEWSA'Happy tears' as council
OL,4,Areorganisation shelved
OL,5,
OL,6,F"They got scared we were coming," joked
OL,7,Fthe Hampshire campaigners whose timing
OL,8,Fcould not have been better.
OL,10,FI travelled with the group from New
OL,11,FForest Together, who had sent a coach
OL,12,Fload of residents to Westminster for a
OL,13,Frally in Parliament Square.
OL,15,FThey had been due to deliver a 32,500
OL,16,Fsignature petition to Downing Street in
OL,17,Fthe afternoon against local government
OL,18,Freorganisation (LGR) in the forest.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,336,330,200,160,0,100
